('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'How did you orchestrate LLM workflows using frameworks like LangChain and multiple foundation models (OpenAI, Anthropic, AWS Bedrock)?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Cloud Architecture & Services", "subcategory": "Cloud & Deployment Architecture", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "CLOUD_INFRASTRUCTURE", "reference_answer": "Deploying AI agents on AWS pairs containerized microservices with managed model endpoints. Agent orchestrators run in Docker containers on Amazon EKS (or ECS Fargate) utilizing Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (HPA) and stateless worker designs. Models are accessed via Amazon Bedrock with PrivateLink VPC endpoints for compliance and IAM least-privilege access. State is persisted in ElastiCache Redis (session state) and RDS/Aurora (checkpointing), with CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray providing distributed tracing and metric alarms.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"name": "Cloud Service Selection & Architecture", "weight": 40, "description": "Identifies appropriate AWS cloud services (Bedrock, EKS, EC2, S3, CloudWatch) for system requirements."}, {"name": "Integration & Security Boundaries", "weight": 30, "description": "Explains IAM roles, VPC networking, encryption, and secure service-to-service communication."}, {"name": "Scalability, Cost & Observability", "weight": 30, "description": "Details CloudWatch monitoring, cost optimization, and high availability design."}], "critical_failures": ["Fails to identify relevant cloud services or explains incorrect architectural interactions.", "Ignores cloud security boundaries, IAM permissions, or monitoring mechanisms."]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-037"}', 1),
