 Orchestrator coordination pattern", "Specialized domain workers with dedicated tools", "Decoupling reasoning from execution"]}, {"id": "C2", "description": "Coordination, State & Communication: Explains how state and message payloads flow between supervisor and domain agents", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Shared state dictionary and context passing", "Structured input/output contracts between agents", "Parallel vs sequential sub-task execution"]}, {"id": "C3", "description": "Validation, Fallback & Escalation: Covers error handling, infinite loop prevention, guardrail validation, and human handoff", "weight": 30, "required": false, "acceptable_evidence": ["Step/depth limits (max iterations)", "Output validation and reflection loops", "Graceful fallback and human escalation"]}], "critical_failures": ["Designs a monolithic prompt instead of specialized agent roles", "Lacks mechanisms to prevent infinite agent execution loops"]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-055"}', 1),
('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Generative AI & LLMs', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'How do you ensure that an LLM agent generates correct SQL queries when interacting with a structured database like Salesforce?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Databases & Caching", "subcategory": "Database & Text-to-SQL Agents", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "TEXT_TO_SQL_AND_DATA", "reference_answer": "Text-to-SQL and data agents operate through a Generate-Validate-Execute-Reflect pattern. 1. Dynamic Schema Ingestion: Relevant table schemas, DDL, and sample foreign keys are retrieved via vector search to protect context window limits. 2. Static Validation: An AST parser (e.g., sqlglot) verifies syntax and strictly enforces read-only SELECT constraints. 3. Sandboxed Execution: Queries run under least-privilege read-only roles with query timeouts. 4. Reflection Loop: Database execution exceptions are fed back into the reasoning loop for iterative self-healing.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"id": "C1", "description": "Schema Context & Prompt Engineering: Explains dynamic DDL pruning and context assembly without context window overflow", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Dynamic schema retrieval using semantic search over DDL", "Injecting foreign key relationships and few-shot exemplars", "Managing token budgets with large enterprise schemas"]}, {"id": "C2", "description": "AST Parsing & Query Safety: Covers query validation, SQL injection prevention, and read-only enforcement", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["AST validation (e.g., sqlglot) to block destructive queries (DROP, DELETE)", "Enforcing read-only permissions and row LIMIT clauses", "Preventing SQL injection through parameterization"]}, {"id": "C3", "description": "Execution & Reflection Self-Correction: Details sandboxed execution and self-healing error correction loops", "weight": 30, "required": false, "acceptable_evidence": ["Executing against read-only replicas with query timeouts", "Feeding database error messages back into the model to self-correct", "Fallback to human data analyst on persistent failures"]}], "critical_failures": ["Allows raw unvalidated SQL generation with write permissions directly against production databases", "Dumps the entire monolithic database schema into the prompt without pruning"]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-056"}', 1),
