('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'How have you used Kubernetes in your projects, and what challenges have you faced while working with container orchestration?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Cloud Architecture & Services", "subcategory": "Cloud & Deployment Architecture", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "CLOUD_INFRASTRUCTURE", "reference_answer": "Deploying AI agents on AWS pairs containerized microservices with managed model endpoints. Agent orchestrators run in Docker containers on Amazon EKS (or ECS Fargate) utilizing Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (HPA) and stateless worker designs. Models are accessed via Amazon Bedrock with PrivateLink VPC endpoints for compliance and IAM least-privilege access. State is persisted in ElastiCache Redis (session state) and RDS/Aurora (checkpointing), with CloudWatch and AWS X-Ray providing distributed tracing and metric alarms.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"name": "Container & Pod Architecture", "weight": 40, "description": "Explains Docker/Kubernetes container orchestration, pod lifecycles, and deployment manifests."}, {"name": "Scaling & Resource Management", "weight": 30, "description": "Details autoscaling (HPA), resource limits, ingress routing, and service discovery."}, {"name": "Operational Reliability & Monitoring", "weight": 30, "description": "Covers health probes, zero-downtime rollouts, and container logging/observability."}], "critical_failures": ["Confuses basic container concepts or fails to explain container orchestration mechanics.", "Lacks understanding of Kubernetes resource allocation, scaling, or health checks."]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-076"}', 1),
