('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'What knowledge sources would you use for building an agentic system that processes database logs?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Databases & Caching", "subcategory": "Database & Text-to-SQL Agents", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "ARCHITECTURE_EXPLANATION", "reference_answer": "Text-to-SQL and data agents operate through a Generate-Validate-Execute-Reflect pattern. 1. Dynamic Schema Ingestion: Relevant table schemas, DDL, and sample foreign keys are retrieved via vector search to protect context window limits. 2. Static Validation: An AST parser (e.g., sqlglot) verifies syntax and strictly enforces read-only SELECT constraints. 3. Sandboxed Execution: Queries run under least-privilege read-only roles with query timeouts. 4. Reflection Loop: Database execution exceptions are fed back into the reasoning loop for iterative self-healing.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"name": "Agent Roles & Coordination", "weight": 40, "description": "Explains agent roles, supervisor/orchestrator responsibilities, and routing mechanisms."}, {"name": "State & Communication", "weight": 30, "description": "Details shared state management, tool usage, and inter-agent message passing."}, {"name": "Validation & Fallback", "weight": 30, "description": "Covers tool validation, retry mechanisms, and human-in-the-loop escalation."}], "critical_failures": ["Describes a single monolithic LLM prompt without agent decomposition or state routing.", "Fails to specify how subagents coordinate or pass execution state."]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-138"}', 1),
