('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'Across your career progression, how has your experience with agentic AI evolved across different projects and roles?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems", "subcategory": "Engineering Leadership & Experience", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "CAREER_PROGRESSION_OWNERSHIP", "reference_answer": "Candidate articulates hands-on engineering experience designing, implementing, and deploying agentic AI systems. Discusses personal technical ownership across prompt engineering, tool integration, orchestration frameworks (e.g., LangGraph), state persistence, and evaluation pipelines. Shares realistic production challenges: debugging non-deterministic failures, mitigating tool calling errors, managing context windows, and iterating from POC prototypes to production-grade deployments with monitoring and guardrails.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"name": "Role Scope & Ownership", "weight": 35, "description": "Describes clear responsibilities, architecture ownership, and system impact in recent roles."}, {"name": "Technical & Cross-functional Leadership", "weight": 35, "description": "Explains engineering decisions, collaboration with stakeholders, 