('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'How do you handle parallel execution of multiple agents, and how do you manage shared memory in such scenarios?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Models & Context Engineering", "subcategory": "Memory & Context Engineering", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "MEMORY_AND_STATE", "reference_answer": "Production agent memory separates short-term working context (active scratchpad within the model''s context window) from long-term persistent storage. Short-term context is optimized using sliding windows, token budgets, and recursive summarization to prevent attention dilution and token exhaustion. Long-term memory persists episodic conversation history and extracted entities (e.g., claim/ticket IDs) in Redis or Vector/Relational databases, retrieving them dynamically via similarity or structured metadata queries.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"id": "C1", "description": "Short-Term vs Long-Term Memory Tiering: Differentiates short-term working context from persistent long-term storage", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Short-term context window buffer vs external database persistence", "Redis for fast session cache", "Vector or relational databases for persistent entity memory"]}, {"id": "C2", "description": "Entity Extraction & Context Injection: Explains entity extraction, indexing, and dynamic context injection techniques", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Structured entity extraction (e.g., claim numbers, user IDs)", "Dynamic injection into system prompts or tool parameters", "Context relevance filtering"]}, {"id": "C3", "description": "Context Window Optimization & Privacy: Covers context window management, compaction, and privacy/retention policies", "weight": 30, "required": false, "acceptable_evidence": ["Sliding window buffering and summarization", "PII sanitization before persisting to long-term storage", "TTL and cache invalidation policies"]}], "critical_failures": ["Claims the entire raw chat history should be injected into every prompt indefinitely", "Cannot distinguish between in-memory session state and persistent storage"]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-223"}', 1),
