ain boundaries", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Supervisor / Orchestrator coordination pattern", "Specialized domain workers with dedicated tools", "Decoupling reasoning from execution"]}, {"id": "C2", "description": "Coordination, State & Communication: Explains how state and message payloads flow between supervisor and domain agents", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Shared state dictionary and context passing", "Structured input/output contracts between agents", "Parallel vs sequential sub-task execution"]}, {"id": "C3", "description": "Validation, Fallback & Escalation: Covers error handling, infinite loop prevention, guardrail validation, and human handoff", "weight": 30, "required": false, "acceptable_evidence": ["Step/depth limits (max iterations)", "Output validation and reflection loops", "Graceful fallback and human escalation"]}], "critical_failures": ["Designs a monolithic prompt instead of specialized agent roles", "Lacks mechanisms to prevent infinite agent execution loops"]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-321"}', 1),
('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'What trade-offs did you consider when iterating from a POC to a more scalable multi-agent system?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Python & Data Manipulation", "subcategory": "AI-Assisted Software Engineering", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "ARCHITECTURE_EXPLANATION", "reference_answer": "AI coding assistants and companion agents (e.g. Cursor, Copilot, automated PR review agents) accelerate development through context-aware autocompletion, boilerplate generation, AST-aware code navigation, and test generation. To prevent regressions, outputs must undergo strict deterministic verification: syntax linting, static analysis, unit test execution, and human code review. Measurable impact is tracked through reduced PR review turnaround time, test coverage improvements, and developer velocity while mitigating risks around hallucinated APIs and security vulnerabilities.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"name": "Agent Roles & Coordination", "weight": 40, "description": "Explains agent roles, supervisor/orchestrator responsibilities, and routing mechanisms."}, {"name": "State & Communication", "weight": 30, "description": "Details shared state management, tool usage, and inter-agent message passing."}, {"name": "Validation & Fallback", "weight": 30, "description": "Covers tool validation, retry mechanisms, and human-in-the-loop escalation."}], "critical_failures": ["Describes a single monolithic LLM prompt without agent decomposition or state routing.", "Fails to specify how subagents coordinate or pass execution state."]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-322"}', 1),
('TECHNICAL', 'AI Engineering', 'Generative AI & LLMs', 'MEDIUM', 'SPECIFIC', 90, 'What trade-offs did you consider when moving from traditional ML systems to generative AI and agent-based architectures?', '{"version": 1, "rubric_version": "142.2", "topic": "Python & Data Manipulation", "subcategory": "AI-Assisted Software Engineering", "question_type": "TECHNICAL_CONCEPT", "question_intent": "CODING_DEVELOPER_PRODUCTIVITY", "reference_answer": "AI coding assistants and companion agents (e.g. Cursor, Copilot, automated PR review agents) accelerate development through context-aware autocompletion, boilerplate generation, AST-aware code navigation, and test generation. To prevent regressions, outputs must undergo strict deterministic verification: syntax linting, static analysis, unit test execution, and human code review. Measurable impact is tracked through reduced PR review turnaround time, test coverage improvements, and developer velocity while mitigating risks around hallucinated APIs and security vulnerabilities.", "evidence_policy": {"acceptable_evidence_is_non_exhaustive": true, "semantic_equivalence_allowed": true, "evaluator_guidance": "acceptable_evidence lists representative examples of valid technical evidence, not mandatory keywords. Any technically equivalent demonstration or alternative valid architecture must receive full credit.", "criteria_weight_policy": "All criteria weights sum to 100 points. Criteria marked required: true represent non-negotiable core competency dimensions that require demonstrative evidence to pass the question. Criteria marked required: false represent architectural depth or operational nuance that additively contribute to the total score."}, "evaluation": {"criteria": [{"id": "C1", "description": "Workflow Integration & Tooling: Explains how coding agents integrate into development environments (IDEs, CI/CD PR bots, AST tools)", "weight": 40, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Integration with IDEs or GitHub PR workflows", "Automating boilerplate, docstrings, or unit tests", "Repository indexing and AST context retrieval"]}, {"id": "C2", "description": "Verification & Quality Assurance: Details verification safeguards before committing AI-generated code", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Mandatory unit test execution and static analysis", "Human-in-the-loop code review approval", "Catching security vulnerabilities or hallucinated APIs"]}, {"id": "C3", "description": "Productivity Metrics & Operational Limitations: Discusses measurable productivity gains and awareness of tool limitations", "weight": 25, "required": false, "acceptable_evidence": ["Tracking metrics like PR turnaround time or test coverage", "Handling context window limits in large mono-repos", "Addressing licensing, privacy, and code IP concerns"]}], "critical_failures": ["Advocates blindly merging AI-generated code without manual review or automated testing", "Cannot explain how coding agents assist software engineering beyond basic string autocompletion"]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-323"}', 1),
