ails typed state schema, message passing, and state reducer functions", "weight": 35, "required": true, "acceptable_evidence": ["Typed state dictionary (TypedDict / Pydantic)", "State reducers (e.g., add_messages) for combining updates", "Maintaining conversation history and tool results in graph state"]}, {"id": "C3", "description": "Persistence & Human-in-the-Loop: Covers checkpointing, human-in-the-loop interrupts, and failure recovery", "weight": 30, "required": false, "acceptable_evidence": ["Checkpointer persistence (Postgres, SQLite, Redis)", "Interrupting before/after nodes for human approval", "State rollback, branching, and time-travel debugging"]}], "critical_failures": ["Asserts LangGraph is strictly a linear pipeline identical to basic LangChain chains", "Cannot explain how state is updated or passed between graph nodes"]}, "question_code": "TECH-AGT-339"}', 1),
